    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_7160a89a",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: grilling-at-grave-site-meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a cemetery with tombstones under a cloudy sky, overlaid with text that reads: 'if you're not grilling at my grave site we were never really friends.' This meme uses a darkly humorous and morbid analogy to express a sense of finality or betrayal in a friendship. The intent is to mock or exaggerate the idea that a friend is not truly loyal or committed if they do not show up at a symbolic 'grave site' to grill. While not explicitly targeting any protected group, the content is potentially harmful as it promotes a cynical, nihilistic view of friendship and could be interpreted as emotionally manipulative or insensitive, especially in contexts where people are grieving or dealing with loss. The humor is derived from the juxtaposition of a solemn, final setting (a cemetery) with a casual, social activity (grilling), creating a jarring and potentially offensive contrast that may be seen as disrespectful or insensitive to those who have lost loved ones.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_0f2fe338"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
